Evaluate $f(x)=\sqrt3\cos x-\sin x$ at the missing values (using exact values of sine and cosine):

- $x=\frac{\pi}{3}$: $\sqrt3\cdot\frac12-\frac{\sqrt3}{2}=0$;
- $x=\frac{5\pi}{6}$: $\sqrt3\cdot\left(-\frac{\sqrt3}{2}\right)-\frac12=-\frac32-\frac12=-2$;
- $x=\frac{7\pi}{6}$: $\sqrt3\cdot\left(-\frac{\sqrt3}{2}\right)-\left(-\frac12\right)=-\frac32+\frac12=-1$;
- $x=\frac{5\pi}{3}$: $\sqrt3\cdot\frac12-\left(-\frac{\sqrt3}{2}\right)=\sqrt3\approx1.7$.

